    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d157">

                <pb facs="0290" n="258" sameAs="frus:frus1958-60v06/pg258"/>

                <head>157. Telegram From the Embassy in Cuba to the Department of State<anchor n="1"
                        xml:id="d157-f1"/></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Havana</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1958-11-17T10:00:00-05:00"><hi rendition="#italic">November 17,
                                1958—10 a.m.</hi></date></dateline></opener>
                <p>509. At conference with Batista November 15, he stated GOC was offered by two
                    American firms large quantities of automatic arms and ammunition. Batista has
                    turned down offers, because he does not want to smuggle arms from US. Batista
                    further believes these arms will now be offered to rebels.</p>
                <p>Although I realize Department is much concerned over flagrant violation of our
                    neutrality laws through consistent supplying of arms and ammunition to rebels
                    from Florida, I again urge that US make every effort in prohibiting this illicit
                    traffic.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#bold">Smith</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
